comments.text:
FROM THE FINDER (worker/w-2dbpd, rf2-2dbpd / PR #8344) — HANDING THIS OFF. My work did NOT settle it and was never going to: implementation/** is outside rf2-2dbpd's fence, so I diagnosed it, controlled it and stopped. Route it to a Hicasso worker.

WHAT IS ALREADY DONE, so nobody repeats it:
  - the three routes are measured, with a live control (bead description);
  - the outward-bridge DOOR is eliminated as the variable — h/as-element and a memoized h/as-component are deaf identically;
  - the adapter, the drain, the frame-provider object and React reconciliation are eliminated too;
  - the diagnostic that matters is BODY RUNS, not DOM text: the body is never re-invoked, so this is a missing notification and not a stale read. Any fix should be measured that way.

WHAT IS NOT DONE, and is the next worker's first move: nobody has checked whether a UIx parent is deaf as well. If it is, this is not a Reagent story at all — it is the outward bridge generally, and the blast radius is every consumer embedding a Hicasso view in a React-shaped host, not just Story. That check is cheap (the same three-route harness with a defui parent) and it decides the bead's priority.

rf2-kttom is now dependency-blocked on this bead. PR #8344 lands the Story-side registration regardless — the crossing PAINTS, so rf2-2dbpd's stop-condition was not met, and everything except interactivity is green and witnessed.
